menu "Protective Stop: lifetime health"

    config DCS_BUTTON_RATED_OPS
        int "Stop switch rated operations (datasheet mechanical life)"
        default 100000
        range 0 1000000000
        help
            Rated mechanical/electrical life of the stop switch on the BOM.
            The default is the NKK Switches FF01 series (FF0126BBCAEA01):
            "Mechanical Life: 100,000 operations minimum; Electrical Life:
            100,000 operations minimum" (FF01 datasheet, Other Ratings).
            The firmware compares the lifetime press counter against this
            and publishes a health warning. Set to your switch's rating if
            you substitute a part. 0 disables the check.

    config DCS_BUTTON_WARN_PCT
        int "Button wear warning threshold (percent of rated operations)"
        default 80
        range 0 99
        help
            GET /api/health reports level WARN once presses reach this
            percentage of DCS_BUTTON_RATED_OPS, and CRITICAL at 100%.
            0 disables the WARN step (CRITICAL still fires at 100%).

    config DCS_MISMATCH_WARN_MIN
        int "Loop-mismatch warning: minimum lifetime events"
        default 50
        range 1 1000000
        help
            A lockstep mismatch is one switch loop reading open while the
            other reads closed on the same tick: contact bounce, a loose
            terminal or a degrading wire. Below this lifetime count the
            rate check is not applied, so a handful of bench events never
            trips a warning.

    config DCS_MISMATCH_WARN_PER_1000
        int "Loop-mismatch warning: events per 1000 presses"
        default 20
        range 0 1000
        help
            Publish WARN when lifetime mismatch events exceed this many per
            1000 presses (presses floored at 1000 for the ratio). 0 disables.

    config DCS_HEALTH_FLUSH_MIN_S
        int "Health counters: minimum seconds between NVS flushes"
        default 60
        range 5 3600
        help
            A dirty counter (new press or mismatch) is written to NVS no
            sooner than this after the previous flush. Bounds flash wear
            and the cache-stall each commit costs both cores.

    config DCS_HEALTH_FLUSH_MAX_S
        int "Health counters: maximum seconds between NVS flushes"
        default 600
        range 30 86400
        help
            Cumulative uptime is written at least this often, so a power
            pull loses at most this much uptime.

endmenu
